{number: 57}
{title: We’ve a Story to Tell}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
We've a [Eb] story to tell to the [Ab] nations,
That shall [Eb] turn their hearts to the [Bb7] right,
A [Eb] story of truth and [Ab] mercy,
A [Eb] story of [Bb7] peace and [Eb] light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For the [Bb7] darkness shall turn to [Eb] dawning,
And the [Bb7] dawning to noonday [Eb] bright,
And [Eb] Christ's great kingdom shall [Ab] come on earth,
The [Eb] kingdom of [Bb7] love and [Eb] light.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
We've a [Eb] song to be sung to the [Ab] nations,
That shall [Eb] lift their hearts to the [Bb7] Lord,
A [Eb] song that shall conquer [Ab] evil
And [Eb] shatter the [Bb7] spear and [Eb] sword.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
We've a [Eb] message to give to the [Ab] nations,
That the [Eb] Lord who reigneth a-[Bb7] bove
Hath [Eb] sent us His Son to [Ab] save us,
And [Eb] show us His [Bb7] heart of [Eb] love.
{end_of_verse}
